WEBVTT

00:00:01.366 --> 00:00:02.471
Most of us spend four to

00:00:02.491 --> 00:00:04.880
five hours a day on a screen.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.968
We plan our careers,

00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:07.661
our health, our money.

00:00:07.681 --> 00:00:10.066
But those hours go unexamined.

00:00:10.982 --> 00:00:12.212
When I left Instagram,

00:00:12.232 --> 00:00:14.542
the leaving felt good at first.

00:00:14.562 --> 00:00:15.630
It was the weeks after that

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.957
were hard.

00:00:16.977 --> 00:00:18.612
The pull back in.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:19.826
A thirty-day wait before

00:00:19.846 --> 00:00:21.946
your account is really gone.

00:00:21.966 --> 00:00:23.246
And a strange quiet,

00:00:23.266 --> 00:00:24.321
where it feels like you're

00:00:24.341 --> 00:00:26.598
missing something important.

00:00:26.618 --> 00:00:27.573
I wrote about all of it,

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.503
in thirteen posts.

00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:31.342
Most apps try to help at

00:00:31.362 --> 00:00:33.236
the moment you open them.

00:00:33.256 --> 00:00:34.361
Almost nothing walks with

00:00:34.381 --> 00:00:36.104
you after you leave.

00:00:36.124 --> 00:00:37.028
So I built three things

00:00:37.048 --> 00:00:38.358
that do.

00:00:39.101 --> 00:00:40.921
A game, for one night.

00:00:40.941 --> 00:00:42.900
A story, for one sitting.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.975
And forty-five days,

00:00:43.995 --> 00:00:45.980
one page at a time.

00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:48.159
First, the game.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.435
It's ten forty-seven at

00:00:49.455 --> 00:00:50.535
night, and your phone is

00:00:50.555 --> 00:00:52.019
still glowing.

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:53.194
You walk out of the feed,

00:00:53.214 --> 00:00:54.394
through four worlds built

00:00:54.414 --> 00:00:55.894
from it, to a quiet beach

00:00:55.914 --> 00:00:57.541
by sunrise.

00:00:57.561 --> 00:00:58.741
Every choice moves four

00:00:58.761 --> 00:01:00.116
meters: focus,

00:01:00.136 --> 00:01:01.316
dopamine, oneness and

00:01:01.336 --> 00:01:02.718
tranquility.

00:01:02.738 --> 00:01:03.518
You don't just choose.

00:01:03.538 --> 00:01:04.812
You act.

00:01:04.832 --> 00:01:05.862
You hold, to set your phone

00:01:05.882 --> 00:01:07.300
face down.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.688
You hold, to break a streak

00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:09.688
of eight hundred and

00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:11.608
forty-seven days.

00:01:11.628 --> 00:01:12.870
You sit through sixty real

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:14.613
seconds of silence.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:15.413
And by morning,

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:16.638
the light you carried shows

00:01:16.658 --> 00:01:18.593
you where you arrived.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.129
Second, the story.

00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:21.785
After the Feed.

00:01:21.805 --> 00:01:22.723
Seven chapters,

00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:24.010
about fifteen minutes,

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.062
built from my own posts.

00:01:26.082 --> 00:01:27.462
Every chapter gives you one

00:01:27.482 --> 00:01:28.948
thing to try.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.161
You add your ordinary

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:31.323
Tuesday to a wall of

00:01:31.343 --> 00:01:32.623
highlights, and watch it

00:01:32.643 --> 00:01:34.477
get seven seconds.

00:01:34.497 --> 00:01:36.530
You fill the hour you get back.

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:37.743
Ten minutes stay unclaimed,

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.232
on purpose.

00:01:39.252 --> 00:01:39.944
You walk through a

00:01:39.964 --> 00:01:41.482
fictional deletion flow,

00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:42.782
and learn each trick by its

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:43.884
name.

00:01:43.904 --> 00:01:45.346
Deactivating and deleting

00:01:45.366 --> 00:01:47.426
are both valid endings.

00:01:47.446 --> 00:01:48.801
And every chapter shows

00:01:48.821 --> 00:01:50.113
what the research actually

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.926
says, with its caveat one

00:01:51.946 --> 00:01:53.409
tap away.

00:01:53.429 --> 00:01:54.584
Because the honest answer

00:01:54.604 --> 00:01:55.914
is this.

00:01:56.244 --> 00:01:57.711
Average effects are small.

00:01:57.731 --> 00:01:59.829
Some people gain a lot.

00:02:00.017 --> 00:02:00.935
You're allowed to find out

00:02:00.955 --> 00:02:02.602
which one you are.

00:02:03.273 --> 00:02:04.303
When the story ends,

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:06.543
it hands you to the third part.

00:02:06.563 --> 00:02:07.593
Forty-five days.

00:02:07.613 --> 00:02:09.544
One short page a day.

00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:10.919
My line, what the research

00:02:10.939 --> 00:02:12.494
says, a small checklist,

00:02:12.514 --> 00:02:14.756
and one thing to do offline.

00:02:14.776 --> 00:02:16.481
Five phases follow the same

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:18.531
arc: notice, take a break,

00:02:18.551 --> 00:02:19.694
slip and decide,

00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:20.731
sit with the quiet,

00:02:20.751 --> 00:02:22.287
and build a rhythm.

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:23.312
It counts the days you

00:02:23.332 --> 00:02:25.804
read. Never days in a row.

00:02:25.824 --> 00:02:26.704
Miss a week, and it won't

00:02:26.724 --> 00:02:28.109
scold you.

00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:29.499
It says, welcome back.

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:31.342
Nothing was lost.

00:02:32.007 --> 00:02:33.450
The story and the series

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.612
never use the tricks they

00:02:34.632 --> 00:02:36.125
warn you about.

00:02:36.145 --> 00:02:36.725
No streaks.

00:02:36.745 --> 00:02:37.350
No accounts.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:38.859
No tracking.

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:39.759
Nothing you type ever

00:02:39.779 --> 00:02:41.417
leaves your device.

00:02:41.437 --> 00:02:42.917
And every page has a line

00:02:42.937 --> 00:02:44.067
to a real person,

00:02:44.087 --> 00:02:45.847
if you need one.

00:02:46.373 --> 00:02:47.141
Play it tonight.

00:02:47.161 --> 00:02:48.503
Read it in one sitting.

00:02:48.523 --> 00:02:50.774
Or start day one tomorrow.

00:02:50.794 --> 00:02:52.554
The links are below.
